mploys approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $100K ranks in the bottom quartile among Basic Materials peers, with revenue growing 17%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $656 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["McEwen Inc. is a small-cap basic materials business with a $733M market cap on $198M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +10% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -15% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 9% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 16% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (18.3% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 519% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":5.188622393636254},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Basic Materials peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Weakness in commodity prices pressures materials companies","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Commodity price volatility and cost-curve position \u2014 in a downturn only the lowest-cost producer has a business, and the rest carry the overhead.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Environmental remediation liability \u2014 tightening regulations on emissions, tailings, and water use create open-ended balance-sheet risk that grows with each legislative cycle.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Trade policy and tariff whiplash \u2014 materials producers are first-order casualties of protectionist swings, and margin gets squeezed from both input and output pricing.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"McEwen (NYSE:MUX) Downgraded by Zacks Research to Strong Sell","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/mcewen-nysemux-downgraded-by-zacks-research-to-strong-sell.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794575251.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["analyst_action"]},{"title":"McEwen (NYSE:MUX) Stock Moved Down to Strong Sell by Zacks Research","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/mcewen-nysemux-stock-moved-down-to-strong-sell-by-zacks-research.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794572663.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.91,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"McEwen Inc. (NYSE:MUX) Analysts Just Slashed Next Year's Revenue Estimates By 16%","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/materials/nyse-mux/mcewen/news/mcewen-inc-nysemux-analysts-just-slashed-next-years-revenue","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794567476.263,"o